From 8da2e2734df0adccc2700fbd85a11348ace4e95e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 10:59:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] player information: the dialog for other skins holds with
 their fonts

The dialog of system/hades (CGUIDialogHadesPlayerInfo, for a skin
without the pages of Hades) names Estuary's fonts: font10, font12,
font20_title, font30_title, font32, font37, Mono26. Another skin may have
none of them, and Kodi then takes its font13 (GUIFontManager::GetFont()),
of a size nobody here knows: a text wider than its label was cut.

make-playerinfo.py now makes every label of the dialog scroll where its
text does not fit (Kodi moves a label only while its text is wider than
it, CGUILabel::Process(): with fonts of Estuary's sizes nothing moves and
nothing is drawn again for it). A label that wraps on two lines takes one
line that scrolls, as two lines of a larger font do not fit its height.
A button scrolls its text only while it has the focus: the button of the
output of this video, whose text keeps its colour with the focus, says
it with a label over it that scrolls. What Estuary says is kept as the
attribute estuary="..." of <scroll>, <wrapmultiline> and the button's
<label>, which Kodi does not read, for the tools that measure the pages
as Estuary shows them. Estuary itself is as it was.

Host test (outside the tree): measure_all.py --font13=36, every font of
the dialog as Estuary's font13 face at 36 px (its 30 px and a fifth
more; neither the tree nor the image has another skin to take as a
reference): before, 146 labels and buttons cut in English and 167 to 172
in Spanish; after, none cut (146 to 172 scroll and are read in full).
With Estuary's fonts nothing changes: 0 that do not fit in en_gb, es_es,
es_ar and es_mx. validate_hades_dialog.py passes.
